{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f17e39d99b57bc5b18", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Semiconductors - Test 2", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 50, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d9249a5d"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d9249a08", "title": "Physics Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b5e6478ae845c43c5ed6"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de5"], "question": {"text": "A light emitting diode (LED) is fabricated using GaAs semiconducting material whose band gap is $1.42 \\mathrm{eV}$. The wavelength of light emitted from the LED is :"}, "options": [{"id": "7b2df4", "text": "$1400 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a2"}, {"id": "92753a", "text": "$650 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a3"}, {"id": "6befbd", "text": "$875 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a4"}, {"id": "318642", "text": "$1243 \\mathrm{~nm}$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470c"], "question": {"text": "<p><strong>Statement I :</strong>&nbsp;When a Si sample is doped with Boron, it becomes P type and when doped by Arsenic it becomes N-type semi conductor such that P-type has excess holes and N-type has excess electrons.</p><p><strong>Statement II :</strong>&nbsp;When such P-type and N-type semi-conductors, are fused to make a junction, a current will automatically flow which can be detected with an externally connected ammeter.</p><p>In the light of above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "2cfa15", "text": "Both Statement I and statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a7"}, {"id": "debde0", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but statement II is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a8"}, {"id": "73ad5a", "text": "Both Statement I and statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499a9"}, {"id": "ab400f", "text": "Statement I is correct but statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499aa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ab", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e39"], "question": {"text": "<math><mi>G</mi><mi>e</mi></math> and <math><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></math> diodes start conducting at <math><mn>0.3</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>V</mi></math> and <math><mn>0.7</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>V</mi></math> respectively. In the following figure if <math><mi>G</mi><mi>e</mi></math> diode connection are reversed, the value of <math><msub><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></math> changes by: (assume that the Ge diode has large breakdown voltage)<br /><br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fyecoopdsbyfuiqfdljbnvxpllnbdupttfeelnpuqixtnfbvxxq.png?alt=media\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "19107b", "text": "<math><mn>0.8</mn><mi> </mi><mi>V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ac"}, {"id": "49a0a2", "text": "<math><mn>0.4</mn><mi> </mi><mi>V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ad"}, {"id": "26858a", "text": "<math><mn>0.2</mn><mi> </mi><mi>V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ae"}, {"id": "5b838e", "text": "<math><mn>0.6</mn><mi> </mi><mi>V</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499af"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a9"], "question": {"text": "If a semiconductor photo diode can detect a photon with a maximum wavelength of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math>, then its band&nbsp;gap energy is: Planck&#39;s constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math>&nbsp;<br />Speed of light&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "b83b10", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b1"}, {"id": "6ea804", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b2"}, {"id": "4e2145", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b3"}, {"id": "04282d", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa392"], "question": {"text": "Consider the following logic circuit.<br/><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FzS7ywEGbj81vSAHFPfa0RFUt6oFeSVnZIJH-YVSY7KQ.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>The output is $\\mathrm{Y}=0$ when :"}, "options": [{"id": "17c845", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}=1$ and $\\mathrm{B}=1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b6"}, {"id": "6dda45", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}=0$ and $\\mathrm{B}=1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b7"}, {"id": "35c8e0", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}=1$ and $\\mathrm{B}=0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b8"}, {"id": "cf2f08", "text": "$\\mathrm{A}=0$ and $\\mathrm{B}=0$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499b9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ba", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b1d"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the circuit shown below, calculate the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></msub><mo>:</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fe0424a4d-c94c-4639-be48-428cfe0a02e8-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 382px; height: 167px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "feb79c", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mA</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499bb"}, {"id": "2ec433", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499bc"}, {"id": "0d270b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499bd"}, {"id": "f5baa0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>05</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499be"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499bf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b5e6478ae845c43c5ed6"], "concepts": ["63f482b98f91a02cddf9f219"], "question": {"text": "The effect of increase in temperature on the number of electrons in conduction band <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></math> and resistance of a semiconductor will be as:"}, "options": [{"id": "8dd7d0", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and resistance decrease", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c0"}, {"id": "7cda92", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and resistance increase", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c1"}, {"id": "f4dc87", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;increases, resistance decreases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c2"}, {"id": "06296a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;decreases, resistance increases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9942"], "question": {"text": "The Boolean expression $\\mathrm{Y}=\\mathrm{A} \\overline{\\mathrm{B}} \\mathrm{C}+\\overline{\\mathrm{A}} \\overline{\\mathrm{C}}$ can be realised with which of the following gate configurations.<br/>A. One 3-input AND gate, 3 NOT gates and one 2input OR gate, One 2-input AND gate,<br/>B. One 3-input AND gate, 1 NOT gate, One 2input NOR gate and one 2-input OR gate<br/>C. 3-input OR gate, 3 NOT gates and one 2-input AND gate<br/>Choose the correct answer from the options given below"}, "options": [{"id": "2ffa6a", "text": "B, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c5"}, {"id": "910622", "text": "A,B Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c6"}, {"id": "33b28f", "text": "A, B, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c7"}, {"id": "67a454", "text": "A, C Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499c9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b650478ae845c43c6900"], "concepts": ["6162fb636ed13040ec84e51f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as <strong>Assertion A</strong> and the other is labelled as <strong>Reason R</strong></p><p><strong>Assertion A:</strong> Diffusion current in a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math> junction is greater than the drift current in magnitude if the junction is forward biased.</p><p><strong>Reason R:</strong> Diffusion current in a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;junction is form the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>-side to the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>-side if the junction is forward biased.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below.</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "679b20", "text": "Both A and R are correct but R is NOT the correct explanation of A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ca"}, {"id": "af0f4b", "text": "A is correct but R is not correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499cb"}, {"id": "f8e3f4", "text": "A is not correct but R is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499cc"}, {"id": "884f83", "text": "Both A and R is correct and R is the correct explanation of A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499cd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ce", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5647"], "question": {"text": "<p>Which of the following statement is not correct in the case of light emitting diodes?</p><p>A. It is a heavily doped p-n junction.</p><p>B. It emits light only when it is forward biased.</p><p>C. It emits light only when it is reverse biased.</p><p>D. The energy of the light emitted is equal to or slightly less than the energy gap of the semiconductor used.</p><p>Choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3c2951", "text": "C and D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499cf"}, {"id": "e53843", "text": "A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d0"}, {"id": "8d22a8", "text": "C", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d1"}, {"id": "8a645a", "text": "B", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d3", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e567dc499d1e49588f9cb7"], "question": {"text": "<p>Identify the logic operation performed by the given circuit.</p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa17d19de-7fa5-4721-bcfd-1ea7d866daa5.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 123px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "9d15e5", "text": "NAND", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d4"}, {"id": "e7af62", "text": "NOR", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d5"}, {"id": "dab877", "text": "OR", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d6"}, {"id": "8f963d", "text": "AND", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d8", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["6117b9d167dbe2603c3eacd5"], "question": {"text": "Choose the correct waveform that can represent the voltage across <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> of the following circuit, assuming the diode is ideal one:<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F73fb6064-ee17-442d-b27e-5837b9b1e678-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 161px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "1b6e8f", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F0f2ea40b-8432-4841-b444-07862a879c1a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 145px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499d9"}, {"id": "2f9b7c", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fdee2a58b-f906-4eb8-90bd-90e246e59ab3-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 143px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499da"}, {"id": "0d3d75", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F460a87f4-4939-4447-bba2-52fdff8cf3e4-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 150px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499db"}, {"id": "518bf7", "text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F3e3e9dc5-e085-4b11-a91b-94add380c97a-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 141px;\" />", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499dc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499dd", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a9"], "question": {"text": "With increasing biasing voltage of a photo diode, the photocurrent magnitude:"}, "options": [{"id": "6a1a81", "text": "remains constant", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499de"}, {"id": "f2d82e", "text": "increases initially and after attaining certain value, it decreases", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499df"}, {"id": "95a332", "text": "increases linearly", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e0"}, {"id": "8a01d3", "text": "increases initially and saturates finally", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e2", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["6117b5e6478ae845c43c5ed6"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5de5"], "question": {"text": "LED is constructed from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>s</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>P</mi></math> semiconducting material. The energy gap of this LED is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi></math>. Calculate the wavelength of light emitted and its colour. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>63</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "1dfa68", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>654</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and red colour", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e3"}, {"id": "2da5df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>654</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and orange colour", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e4"}, {"id": "4acb0b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1046</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and red colour", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e5"}, {"id": "9e36f3", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1046</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math> and blue colour", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e7", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4759"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e39"], "question": {"text": "For using a multimeter to identify diode from electrical components, choose the correct statement out of the following about the diode"}, "options": [{"id": "5ba561", "text": "It is two terminal device which conducts current in both directions.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e8"}, {"id": "a82ee3", "text": "It is two terminal device which conducts current in one direction only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499e9"}, {"id": "3dbcf2", "text": "It does not conduct current gives an initial deflection which decays to zero.", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ea"}, {"id": "9ca5ff", "text": "It is three terminal device which conducts current in one direction only between central terminal and either of the remaining two terminals", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499eb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ec", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e567c5499d1e49588f9963"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa392"], "question": {"text": "<p>Identify the logic operation performed by the given circuit&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F01be7a3e-ad14-4ccb-936b-063bd980a113-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 151px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "b615f2", "text": "AND gate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ed"}, {"id": "5ee0bb", "text": "OR gate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ee"}, {"id": "238056", "text": "NOR gate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499ef"}, {"id": "0c2e36", "text": "NAND gate", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f1", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5670"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80a9"], "question": {"text": "<p>Conductivity of a photodiode starts changing only if the wavelength of incident light is less than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>660</mn><mo> </mo><mi>nm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The band gap of photodiode is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo> </mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi></math> is:</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1d2da6", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f2"}, {"id": "d40269", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f3"}, {"id": "d688c9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f4"}, {"id": "79b68b", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>21</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2d2ee0e063d92499f6", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60e2fadb66f9ce3f243b4798"], "topics": ["60e2fa